# Plugin version bump

Canonical rule: `rules/dev/plugin-version-bump.md` (shared by Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex).

**After changing shipped plugin content** (`skills/`, `hooks/`, `agents/`, manifests, `scripts/`):

1. Bump `version` in **all three** manifests (`.claude-plugin/`, `.cursor-plugin/`, `.codex-plugin/`) + `README.md` badges — same semver in one commit.
2. Update `CHANGELOG.md` under the new `[X.Y.Z]` section.
3. Open a PR; after merge run the Release workflow to create `vX.Y.Z` (CI requires manifest ↔ tag match).
4. Users need `/plugin marketplace update tamirs-plugins` then `/plugin update tamirs-superpowers@tamirs-plugins` — `/reload-plugins` alone only reloads cache.

Pushing commits without a version bump does **not** update installed Claude Code plugins.
